WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.619
<v U_UKN>It's important to have a comprehensive approach to maintaining the CIA Triad

2
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.200
<v U_UKN>confidentiality, integrity and availability.

3
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.559
<v U_UKN>These are the foundations of the cybersecurity domain

4
00:00:21.569 --> 00:00:24.420
<v U_UKN>Confidentiality means that no private information

5
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.100
<v U_UKN>has been disclosed to unauthorized individuals.

6
00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:29.860
<v U_UKN>We need to ensure that personally identifiable

7
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.319
<v U_UKN>information also known as PI I is protected

8
00:00:34.009 --> 00:00:35.950
<v U_UKN>if you are part of a security team,

9
00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:38.200
<v U_UKN>your goal is to protect the assets or

10
00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:41.580
<v U_UKN>the information of large corporations or multiple individuals.

11
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.950
<v U_UKN>For example, if you work in banking health care or insurance companies,

12
00:00:45.959 --> 00:00:48.750
<v U_UKN>you have multiple personal identifiers to protect

13
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.419
<v U_UKN>Integrity,

14
00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.080
<v U_UKN>ensures that this information is not being corrupted

15
00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.560
<v U_UKN>or changed without the information owner's permission.

16
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.830
<v U_UKN>It confirms that the information being maintained is complete and

17
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.349
<v U_UKN>accurate and consistent with the legitimate use of that information.

18
00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:08.559
<v U_UKN>Interfering with the integrity of information can have serious ramifications.

19
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.239
<v U_UKN>For example, someone without authority changes someone's medical information

20
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:14.959
<v U_UKN>and now a patient may be in

21
00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.959
<v U_UKN>jeopardy because someone changed that vital information.

22
00:01:19.169 --> 00:01:21.629
<v U_UKN>Our job is to maintain the security of that

23
00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:25.230
<v U_UKN>information so that no one unless authorized to do so

24
00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:28.190
<v U_UKN>changes any part of the information we are protecting

25
00:01:29.029 --> 00:01:33.459
<v U_UKN>availability is critical because it is essential that authorized users

26
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.569
<v U_UKN>have access to important information in a timely manner.

27
00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:41.669
<v U_UKN>Cyber attacks that disrupt services often target the availability of data.

28
00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:41.959
<v U_UKN>A

29
00:01:42.269 --> 00:01:45.410
<v U_UKN>business cannot function if its employees and customers

30
00:01:45.419 --> 00:01:48.089
<v U_UKN>cannot access their information in a timely manner.

31
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.239
<v U_UKN>A ransomware attack, for example,

32
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:55.500
<v U_UKN>may lock up a system and block access to vital information and services

33
00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:59.300
<v U_UKN>that access will not be restored until a payment is made.

